Here's my current set of diffs against 2.2.11-pre1 --

  (1) Update the asn drop I gave you to my second try.  Tweek _that_
      to avoid an asn wrap detection problem.  Ug.

  (2) Give -fno-strict-alias to gcc 2.95.  No matter what we do for
      2.3, we won't be going back to fix what needs fixing in 2.2.

  (3) Code drop from Jay: PYXIS, DP264, profiling.

  (4) osf_getsysinfo and spin_trylock patchlets from Jeff Garzik.

  (5) The cvtqt/m emulation failed on 0 input.  This broke floor
      in glibc 2.1 on ev4.

  (6) Yellowfin alignment bug fix.


r~

