> cd /usr/lib
> ln -s libguile.so.4 libguile.so.2
> and continue the install from there.
>

That's the right hack for executables but not for rpm. The rpm hack
is to add libguile.so.2 in a virtual provides line in /etc/rpmrc:

	Provides: libguile.so.2

Or just add --nodeps to the command line.

You might want to just recompile in order to get the correct dependence

