Since you are already working with an external box the easiest thing 
is to get a bigger external box. While it is true that "scsi" 
external boxes are expensive there is a cheaper solution. What I did 
for one of our netware servers is take an extra pc tower case and use 
that as an external scsi cdrom box in this case. Check one of the 
cable places for a pc case rear slot cover that has an external scsi 
connector on the outside and a male 50 pin connector on the inside. I 
have a standard submini 50 pin scsi cable connected to the outside 
and internally I have a standard 50 pin ribbon cable. Of course this 
is all standard scsi but there is no reason you couldn't do the same 
thing with fast or wide, just different connectors. I got the slot 
cover adaptor at a local computer show, they had several different 
styles. The adaptor was about $15 and a standard pc tower case is 
down to $40 since ATX is taking over. Alot cheaper than any of the 
official scsi boxes I have seen. Any one see any reason it wouldn't 
work just as well? I have had "official" scsi boxes and there is 
nothing special about them except maybe a dip switch for id setting.

