I have a small network with IP masq.  setup.  I have a direct connection to
the internet as well with a static ip.  The way i have it all configured
would be.  computer A B C D with ip addresses of 192.168.0.x and computer E
with the static IP address.  All computers can route out.  I have computer E
setup as my main webserver running apache.  I want to be able to assign host
names to all the computers in the network so that i can contact each one by
typing its corrisponding host name example "A.something.com"
"B.something.com"  How would i set this up so that i can assign host names
to the internal network that can be accessed from the outside?  thanks for
the help


