>            1806347 = 1904804 ?   Must be the new math.

I don't know too much about ext2, but could 100K blocks be reserved for
the superuser?
This is the usual 5% reservation for the overhead. You can change this 
value by using tunefs -minfree #  , though I would not recommend it because 
you will have to pay for it. You can optimize this value in for size/speed 
of the filesystem.

Only my 0.02$

