kinetics (in C).  I need high precision when running numerical
integration
techniques but must still be able to run many, many iterations.  With 64
bits, I can use single precision floating point in place of double
precision, giving me an added speed advantage without sacrificing
precision, or I can be more precise by sticking with double and not
sacrifice speed.

