Briefly, summary of problem. My LX164 (from Compusys) had been running
away happily
for several months without a problem until yesterday when the qlogic
isp1040 scsi controller
started playing up (either that or its a problem with the driver in
2.2.10, but seeing as i'd had
35 days uptime with it, i doubt it). Anyway, I rebooted and actually
turned the machine off
for the first time this year. Now problems start. Previously I'd booted
off a milo floppy from
SRM - not a brilliant idea but i'd never got round to changing it. Today
i found that the floppy
drive had given up as well as the qlogic (probably got a lot to do with
the amount of dust in
the room, which has recently had the windows replaced and two walls
removed!). This made
me decide to switch to ARC/AlphaBios, as my primary system disk is ide
(so i cant boot
straight from srm). However, when following the (now outdated) links at
digital's web site
(www.windows.digital.com/support/sysopt.htp no longer exists), I can
only see referenced
AlphaBioses for specific dec systems. Does anyone know where to get
something like
a generic LX164 arc/alphabios?	

cheers
john


